##DESCRIPTION
## Find the margin of error and point estimate for a population proportion 
## confidence interval.
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Confidence intervals)
## DBsection(Concepts)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Jessie Oehrlein)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('confidence interval', 'proportion', 'margin of error', 'point estimate')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$length = random(0.05, 0.3,  0.01);
$mean   = random(0.15, 0.85, 0.01);

BEGIN_PGML
A confidence interval for a population proportion is [`([$mean-0.5*$length],[$mean+0.5*$length])`]. 

a)  Determine the margin of error. [_]{Real(0.5*$length)}

b)  Find the point estimate. [_]{Real($mean)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) Given a confidence interval, the margin of error is half it's length.  In this case its
[``` \frac{[$mean+0.5*$length] - [$mean-0.5*$length]}{2} = [$length/2] ```]

b) The point estimate will be the midpoint of the interval ends or 
[```  \frac{[$mean+0.5*$length] + [$mean-0.5*$length]}{2} = [$mean] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.